5th. When an operation was being performed upon the baby, &ldquo;Harriet
      stood by, narrowly observing all that was done, but, to the astonishment
      of the operator, betraying not the smallest sign of emotion.&rdquo;

After Shelley's (conjectured) visit to Harriet at Bath&mdash;8th of
      June to 18th&mdash;&ldquo;it seems to have been arranged that Shelley
      should henceforth join the Skinner Street household each day at dinner.&rdquo;
